the knowledge base module_a2_cross_cutting_examples includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/module-a2-cross-cutting-examples.l4".

the practicable days for a timing is a number if
    immediate is equal to the timing
    and the number is equal to 1
    otherwise prompt is equal to the timing
    and the number is equal to 7
    otherwise reasonable is equal to the timing
    and the number is equal to 14
    otherwise extended is equal to the timing
    and the number is equal to 30.

the to calendar days for a business days B is a number N if
    N = B * 7 / 5.

the ten business days is a number if
    the to calendar days for 10 is the number.

